# Root .dockerignore — applied to every build whose context is the repo root
# (api, bot, miniapp). The per-app .dockerignore files next to each Dockerfile
# are NOT consulted when the build context is the repo root — Docker only reads
# the .dockerignore at the context root. So this is the one that actually matters.

# Node / pnpm
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.venv
**/venv

# Env (never copy real secrets into images; .env.example is fine to keep — explicit allow)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local infra state
infrastructure/prod/.env

# VCS / IDE / OS junk
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.claude

# Plans and developer notes (no need to ship to images)
plans/
**/*.md.bak
